# --- ETK PROJECT GITIGNORE ---

# 1. Ignore the Shader Vault (Relative paths)
# This stops those massive .dat and .SELF files from hitting GitHub
vault/
**/vault/

# 1b. Ignore the Tier-B host snapshot tree (addendum: install.sh backs up
# rig-side telemetry ledgers, tuned RPCS3 configs, and the RPCS3 user-profile
# tree — saves, trophies, .rap licenses — here on every install run).
# Mirrors the vault/ precedent: never auto-deleted, never committed.
state/
**/state/

# 1c. Belt-and-suspenders guard: the operator-friendly `screenshots/` is
# a symlink to `state/screenshots/` (see addendum convention — Tier-B
# mutable state lives under `state/`). If someone deletes the symlink
# and recreates a real dir by accident, this keeps PNG captures out of
# the repo regardless.
/screenshots
/screenshots/

# 2. Ignore Live Data / Shared Memory
# We don't want to track etk_mode.txt or the command queue
shm/
**/shm/

# 2b. Probe capture output — scripts/etk_probe.sh writes timestamped CSVs to
# $ETK_ROOT/etk_probe at runtime (thermal-calibration sweeps). Runtime data,
# same precedent as vault/ and state/ — never committed. The historical
# 20260521 captures were archived under _archive/etk_probe/ (also ignored).
etk_probe/
**/etk_probe/

# 3. macOS Pollution
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*

# 4. System & Editor Caches
*.log
*.tmp
*.swp
__pycache__/
.vscode/

# 5 Ignore the dev _archive
_archive/

# 5a. os-install holds multi-GB .img.gz payloads AND the Tier-I image lane's
# build scripts. A blanket /os-install ignore was protecting the payloads and
# taking the recipe with it: build_gtk_image_v2.sh bakes a SHIPPED RELEASE
# ASSET and was tracked in no repository at all — it existed only on the
# laptop, so no other machine could run the lane (etk-cloud could not,
# 2026-08-05). Ignore the payloads, keep the recipe.
/os-install/*
!/os-install/build/
/os-install/build/*
!/os-install/build/*.sh
!/os-install/build/*.md

# 5b. Design dossiers — LOCAL-PRIVATE, never committed. The dossiers/ tree
# lives at $ETK_ROOT/dossiers as the design-rationale archive (referenced
# throughout the code as `dossiers/<Name>Dossier.md` and inline `dossier §N`
# citations). Pulled from the public repo 2026-06-14; stays local only —
# same precedent as vault/ and state/. Their absence from git is expected;
# the dangling references are design provenance, not missing files.
dossiers/

# 5c. Host-side forensic capture sets (GPU-wedge redumps, devcoredumps,
# frozen-frame grabs) and pulled bog-profiler sample sets — runtime data,
# same precedent as vault/ and state/. Analyzed locally, never committed.
manual_forensics/
bog_samples/

# 5d. Local video captures (session recordings, hundreds of MB) — never
# committed; docs/screenshots/ (small PNGs) remains tracked.
docs/video/

# 6. Operator config — generated locally by install.sh's first-run
# wizard. Tracks the rig SSH target, build tier, HUD preferences, etc.
# The canonical template is `etk.conf.example` (committed).
etk.conf
# Hand-made backups of the operator config (e.g. etk.conf.bak-pre-perfstat)
etk.conf.bak*

# 7. Claude Code machine-local settings — personal, not shared. The `.claude/`
# dir stays at the project root (Claude Code requires it there); only the
# per-machine local settings file is untracked.
.claude/settings.local.json

# PADDOCK known_repo game-source pointers — PRIVATE, must never be published
# (keeps NPS/pkg URLs out of the public index = the defensibility line).
# The .example template is tracked; the filled-in real file is not.
config/paddock_repos.json

# Pro Tuning build artifacts
pro-tuning/dist/
# Driver catalog = local staging only (binaries never committed; same precedent
# as vault/). Covers ROCKNIX glibc ICDs (drivers/*.so) AND the Android
# adrenotools packages staged for the aPS3e side (drivers/android/*).
drivers/*.so
drivers/**/*.so
drivers/**/*.zip
drivers/android/
/emulators/

# Forge staging sidecars (forge.sh): sha manifests + .prev backups of replaced
# artifacts. Local provenance only — the artifacts themselves are already
# ignored above; these ride along with them.
drivers/*.sha256
drivers/*.prev
*.forge-tmp
